From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:30:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 618/619] phy: mediatek: tphy: let a U2 port name its squelch
 threshold

u2_phy_instance_init() writes a squelch threshold of 2 to every U2 port.
On the MT6797's USB11 port that fails: a full-speed keyboard that the
vendor kernel enumerates gets -EPROTO on every first control transfer.
Register dumps of the two kernels differ in the PHY only in that field,
8 under the vendor kernel, which leaves the hardware default.

Read an optional mediatek,rx-sqth per port and keep 2 without it. The
property is parsed in xlate, before phy_init, like the other per-port
settings.
---
 drivers/phy/mediatek/phy-mtk-tphy.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/mediatek/phy-mtk-tphy.c b/drivers/phy/mediatek/phy-mtk-tphy.c
index 41025a345..61263980f 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/mediatek/phy-mtk-tphy.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/mediatek/phy-mtk-tphy.c
@@ -342,6 +342,7 @@ struct mtk_phy_instance {
 	int eye_term;
 	int intr;
 	int discth;
+	u32 rx_sqth;
 	int pre_emphasis;
 	bool bc12_en;
 	bool force_b_session_valid;
@@ -868,7 +869,8 @@ static void u2_phy_instance_init(struct mtk_tphy *tphy,
 	/* DP/DM BC1.1 path Disable */
 	mtk_phy_clear_bits(com + U3P_USBPHYACR6, PA6_RG_U2_BC11_SW_EN);
 
-	mtk_phy_update_field(com + U3P_USBPHYACR6, PA6_RG_U2_SQTH, 2);
+	mtk_phy_update_field(com + U3P_USBPHYACR6, PA6_RG_U2_SQTH,
+			     instance->rx_sqth);
 
 	/* Workaround only for mt8195, HW fix it for others (V3) */
 	u2_phy_pll_26m_set(tphy, instance);
@@ -1166,6 +1168,8 @@ static void phy_parse_property(struct mtk_tphy *tphy,
 				 &instance->intr);
 	device_property_read_u32(dev, "mediatek,discth",
 				 &instance->discth);
+	instance->rx_sqth = 2;
+	device_property_read_u32(dev, "mediatek,rx-sqth", &instance->rx_sqth);
 	device_property_read_u32(dev, "mediatek,pre-emphasis",
 				 &instance->pre_emphasis);
 	dev_dbg(dev, "bc12:%d, src:%d, vrt:%d, term:%d, intr:%d, disc:%d\n",
-- 
